.TH FILE 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
file \- determine file type
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B file
.I name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I File
classifies each argument and prints its name and description.
The test on maux is the ProDOS storage type and file-type byte only;
it does not examine the contents or guess a programming language.
.PP
Directories are identified before the type-byte lookup.
Known types include text, binary, system program, Applesoft and Integer
BASIC programs, Applesoft variables, relocatable object, Pascal area,
AppleTalk file and GS/OS application.
An unrecognized type is printed as a hexadecimal byte.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/FILE  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ls(1), nm(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 if all files were described, 1 if any cannot be examined, 2 if no operands were supplied.
.SH BUGS
Type labels are metadata, not content validation. In particular the REL label in this tool's table is type $FE; a NAS $F8 REL object currently prints as an unknown type.
